00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:02.941
So if we go back to the, the deck.

00:24:03.043 --> 00:24:09.430
So, um, branch protections actually, um-

00:24:11.796 --> 00:24:17.563
So what they do is you configure the
branch that you want to only be mergeable

00:24:17.563 --> 00:24:22.109
into based on, um, a specific CI check.

00:24:22.411 --> 00:24:26.676
So failed checks equals merge
button is disabled, so it catches

00:24:26.679 --> 00:24:28.798
the regression in the specific PR.

00:24:29.497 --> 00:24:36.009
Um, it, you know, blocks on failure
and only allows the merge button

00:24:36.021 --> 00:24:38.414
to be even clicked when it passes.

00:24:38.691 --> 00:24:44.116
So, um, there's a second type of
branch protection, which requires the

00:24:44.117 --> 00:24:51.533
branch to be updated to the, um, to
the latest copy of the target branch.

00:24:51.577 --> 00:24:56.495
So what that enforces is, um,
that your code integrates with

00:24:56.617 --> 00:25:00.764
other people's code fine without
causing any regressions as well.

00:25:01.186 --> 00:25:06.075
So the failure gate only stops your
bug, but requiring the branch to be

00:25:06.076 --> 00:25:10.079
updated stops someone else's merge
work from interacting with yours,

00:25:10.575 --> 00:25:15.948
and it reruns the scan on that
combination before it can even merge.

00:25:16.254 --> 00:25:19.821
Now, I'm not gonna show the branch
protection right now because that

00:25:19.823 --> 00:25:24.162
differs per repo and per, um, user.

00:25:24.465 --> 00:25:28.984
So… But know that you have to
configure this at the repo level as

00:25:28.984 --> 00:25:30.612
opposed to being in the scan level.

00:25:30.635 --> 00:25:33.486
Otherwise, the gate
doesn't function at all.

