CI gate runs, the scan fails,

00:34:36.245 --> 00:34:37.375
and the merge is blocked.

00:34:37.410 --> 00:34:38.306
We just looked at that.

00:34:38.317 --> 00:34:42.105
There is no way to click that merge
button if these scans are failed.

00:34:42.167 --> 00:34:45.096
Now, that is enforced at
the branch protection level.

00:34:45.852 --> 00:34:51.634
Um, and so on the WordPress site, same
gate, but it's a little bit different.

00:34:51.672 --> 00:34:55.471
So after the branch gets opened,
it actually deploys it to staging.

00:34:56.520 --> 00:35:00.058
Um, this is where it actually
scans on the staging site.

00:35:00.114 --> 00:35:03.078
And again, we saw gate blocked.

00:35:03.230 --> 00:35:05.162
So check went red.

00:35:05.325 --> 00:35:07.477
You can no longer click that merge button.

00:35:08.211 --> 00:35:11.176
Um, there's als- you can also
potentially gate the release.

00:35:11.462 --> 00:35:14.705
Uh, I don't have an example here because
this plugin isn't available anywhere,

00:35:14.705 --> 00:35:19.777
but if you wanna talk to me about
that, reach out on socials, GitHub.

00:35:19.977 --> 00:35:24.542
You know, we can figure out how
to set this up in your CI system.

00:35:25.069 --> 00:35:28.616
So we will quickly talk about
what actually gets caught here.

00:35:29.390 --> 00:35:34.141
Things that we can catch automatically
with axe-core is missing labels, alt

00:35:34.151 --> 00:35:39.701
text, contrast problems, um, keyboard
reachability, structural ARIA issues,

00:35:40.167 --> 00:35:43.557
and, you know, you're gonna catch
regressions the moment the code

00:35:43.557 --> 00:35:45.810
lands, not when it reaches production.

00:35:46.413 --> 00:35:50.942
But what still needs a human is
logical reading order, screen reader

00:35:50.952 --> 00:35:56.873
UX quality, cognitive load and plain
language, and any claim of WCAG

00:35:56.931 --> 00:36:00.459
level conformance is gonna have to
have a human do the checking, so…

00:36:01.191 --> 00:36:03.500
Automation catches structural issues.

00:36:03.727 --> 00:36:06.153
Accessibility is, uh,
much broader than that.

00:36:06.174 --> 00:36:10.263
You do still need manual testing
and real user feedback after this.

00:36:11.196 --> 00:36:14.515
But, so what the passing check hides.

00:36:14.848 --> 00:36:17.857
So some things are not actually your bug.

00:36:17.904 --> 00:36:18.995
We were just talking about this.

00:36:19.035 --> 00:36:22.017
If you're scanning someone
else's website, if you build a

00:36:22.020 --> 00:36:23.959
plugin, you don't own that site.

00:36:23.959 --> 00:36:27.354
You have no control over what the
theme problems are, what content are.

00:36:27.667 --> 00:36:31.810
You need to decide upfront if those
theme problems block the release.

00:36:32.290 --> 00:36:37.790
And if you decide that the theme problems
should, I feel like probably in the near

00:36:37.790 --> 00:36:42.499
future, you're gonna wanna skip these
checks and ignore them, which that means

00:36:42.499 --> 00:36:43.901
they're not gonna be useful for anyone.

00:36:44.852 --> 00:36:48.732
Um, Configured does not mean conformant.

00:36:48.825 --> 00:36:52.212
So a green check means that
what you have configured passes.

00:36:52.486 --> 00:36:55.290
You know, in the scan we done,
we didn't check heading order

00:36:55.348 --> 00:36:56.596
because it's a best practice.

00:36:57.098 --> 00:37:00.906
Um, placeholders pass the accessibility
name check, but you might wanna enforce

00:37:00.917 --> 00:37:03.337
visible placeholders or visible labels.

00:37:03.738 --> 00:37:07.508
So axe only checks what you've
configured, the specific rules for it.

00:37:07.877 --> 00:37:09.350
Takes deliberate setup.

00:37:10.156 --> 00:37:13.970
And in this entire system, there is
no baseline feature built out yet.

00:37:14.013 --> 00:37:19.053
If you wanna start using this, you need
to scope tightly to just the elements

00:37:19.056 --> 00:37:23.113
that you're wanting to check and widen
it over time, or you will need to start

00:37:23.113 --> 00:37:25.040
with a low threshold, tighten it later.

00:37:25.344 --> 00:37:29.375
